<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Portable Google Cast integration for the OpenBurnBar Windows port
    (Phase 4 · Integrations · Google Cast lane).

    This is the DEPENDENCY-FREE, platform-agnostic half of the Cast feature: the
    CASTV2 protobuf wire framing, the DNS-SD (_googlecast._tcp) mDNS record
    parse/build, the receiver protocol state machine + payload builders, the
    reconnect/recovery planner, the discovery merge/dedup, and the setup-wizard
    state machine + view-model. It has NO Windows / WinUI dependency on purpose —
    the SAME managed assembly is:
      • referenced by the net8.0-windows adapter
        (OpenBurnBar.Integrations.Cast.Windows), which supplies the real TLS
        socket + live Dnssd browser behind interfaces, AND
      • unit-tested on the macOS authoring host today via `dotnet test`
        (windows/tests/integrations-cast), exactly the pattern already proven by
        the Presentation / Switcher / Dashboard portable libraries.

    Parity sources (macOS AgentLens/Services/Cast/):
      • CastMessageFraming.swift            -> Protocol/CastMessage.cs + CastFraming.cs
      • CastChannelClient.swift             -> Protocol/CastReceiverProtocol.cs
                                               + Protocol/CastInboundRouter.cs
                                               + Session/CastReceiverStateMachine.cs
      • CastDevice.swift                    -> Model/CastDevice.cs
      • CastDiscovery.swift                 -> Discovery/CastTxtRecord.cs
                                               + Discovery/CastCapabilities.cs
                                               + Discovery/CastDiscoveryMerge.cs
                                               + Discovery/DnsWire.cs
                                               + Discovery/CastMdnsAdvertisement.cs
                                               + Discovery/DnsSdBrowseQuery.cs
                                               + Discovery/ICastServiceBrowser.cs
      • CastReconnectStrategy.swift         -> Session/CastReconnectPlanner.cs
      • CastTLSConnection.swift             -> Session/ICastSocket.cs (the socket seam)
      • CastWizardModel.swift               -> Wizard/CastWizardStateMachine.cs
                                               + Wizard/CastWizardViewModel.cs
      • HomeAssistantCastRecoveryClient.swift -> Recovery/HomeAssistantRecoveryPayload.cs

    Targets net8.0 so the net8.0-windows adapter can reference it, while the
    net10.0 test project can reference it too (a lower TFM is consumable by a
    higher one). TreatWarningsAsErrors keeps the port honest.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>disable</ImplicitUsings>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <RootNamespace>OpenBurnBar.Integrations.Cast</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>OpenBurnBar.Integrations.Cast</AssemblyName>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
